// Test: bugfixes/pairs_boxed_into_any_is_an_object
// Grammar: variable_declaration (any), function_call (json.encode)
// Semantic: BOXED_ANY_ABI.md §2, §3.3 — a pairs value stored into an `any`
//   is a tag-6 (Object) box holding its JSON-tree object
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
//   {"name":"ab"}
//   {"code":"xyz","city":"Lima"}
//
// Regression: the box got tag 1 (integer), so the `any` read back as the
// address of the converted object: json.encode printed a number.

start:
	pairs<string, string> ab = {"name": "ab"}
	any boxed = ab
	print(json.encode(boxed))
	pairs<string, string> place = {"code": "xyz", "city": "Lima"}
	any other = place
	print(json.encode(other))
